messages.content:
You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: C08
Scenario title: Child Activity Enrollment and Schedule Changes
Initial workflow description:
I find an activity for my child, sign up if it fits, and put it on our calendar. If the provider changes the schedule, I rearrange our plans.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "What sources or platforms do you use to discover available activities for your child — for example, a specific community website, a provider app, email newsletters, or social media?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "What specific criteria do you evaluate to decide whether an activity is a good fit — such as cost, location, time slot, the child's age eligibility, or conflicts with other commitments?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "How does the enrollment step actually work — do you complete an online form, make a phone call, pay a fee, or do something else, and does it require approval or agreement from another parent or guardian?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "Which calendar system do you use to track the activity schedule, and is it shared with other family members who also need to see or act on changes?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "How do you typically receive notification of a schedule change from the activity provider — for example, via email, a text message, an app notification, or a phone call?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "When a provider's schedule change conflicts with an existing family commitment, what do you do — for example, do you cancel the enrollment, look for an alternative session, or contact the provider to negotiate?"
  }
]
Reference workflow for oracle use:
{
  "goal": "Child Activity Enrollment and Schedule Changes with explicit responsibilities, decisions and recorded completion.",
  "actors": [
    "mother",
    "partner",
    "activity provider",
    "transport caregiver"
  ],
  "systems": [
    "provider registration page",
    "shared family calendar",
    "registration receipt folder",
    "family messaging app"
  ],
  "inputs": [
    "activity schedule",
    "household availability",
    "provider participation requirements",
    "household spending limit"
  ],
  "outputs": [
    "participation decision",
    "registration confirmation",
    "transport assignment",
    "updated calendar notice"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "name": "Collect the activity schedule and participation requirements",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "name": "Check household and transport caregiver availability",
      "actor": "partner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "name": "Compare the activity cost with the spending limit",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "name": "Confirm the participation decision with the partner",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "name": "Submit the approved registration request",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "name": "Save provider confirmation before marking enrollment complete",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "name": "Assign transport and add the activity to the calendar",
      "actor": "partner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A8",
      "name": "Confirm revised arrangements after a provider schedule change",
      "actor": "mother"
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "condition": "Do schedule and cost fit the household's agreed constraints?",
      "branches": [
        "parent may approve registration",
        "choose another time or decline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "condition": "Has the provider confirmed enrollment or the revised schedule?",
      "branches": [
        "update the calendar and notify caregivers",
        "keep the arrangement pending and contact the provider"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": [
    "activity fully booked",
    "registration confirmation missing",
    "transport caregiver unavailable",
    "provider schedule change"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from": "A1",
      "to": "A2",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A2",
      "to": "A3",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A3",
      "to": "A4",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A4",
      "to": "A5",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A5",
      "to": "A6",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A6",
      "to": "A7",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A7",
      "to": "A8",
      "type": "control_flow"
    }
  ],
  "automation_opportunities": [
    {
      "target": "A2",
      "rationale": "Flag calendar conflicts and missing transport availability."
    },
    {
      "target": "A6",
      "rationale": "Track unconfirmed registration requests."
    },
    {
      "target": "A8",
      "rationale": "Draft calendar changes and caregiver notifications."
    }
  ],
  "operating_context": {
    "frequency": "enrollment considered at the start of a term, with occasional provider changes",
    "manual_effort": "Checking schedules and completing a request takes about fifteen minutes in this fictional household.",
    "data_availability": "Requirements and availability are shown on the provider page; confirmation is saved separately by the family.",
    "integration_and_approval_constraints": "Registration and payments need parent approval; a suggested calendar entry is not evidence of provider confirmation."
  },
  "interpretation": "Activity dependencies describe the nominal sequence. Decision branches and exception descriptions qualify that sequence; this is not an executable BPMN model."
}
Task: Simulate a concise domain expert who answers only these questions using the reference workflow.
Do not reveal the full reference workflow. Do not add details not needed by the questions.
If a requested fact is absent, explicitly say it is not specified; do not guess.
Use at most 80 words per answer. Return one answer for each question, with matching ID and question text.
Return JSON: {"answers": [{"question_id": "Q1", "question": "original question", "answer": "grounded answer"}]}
